  "text": "That sounds like a lovely gesture! A classic breakfast omelette is a great choice for a surprise breakfast in bed. It's simple, delicious, and can be customized to your mom's preferences. Here's a basic recipe for a classic breakfast omelette:\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udf73 Classic Breakfast Omelette Recipe\n\n#### \ud83c\udf73 Ingredients (serves 1):\n- 2 large eggs\n- 1/4 cup milk or cream (optional, for fluffiness)\n- 1/2 teaspoon salt\n- 1/4 teaspoon black pepper\n- 1 tablespoon butter (or oil for a lighter option)\n- Optional fillings: cooked bacon, shredded cheese, diced ham, spinach, tomatoes, mushrooms, or fresh herbs like chives or parsley\n\n#### \ud83e\uddf0 Instructions:\n1. **Crack the eggs into a bowl** and whisk them with a fork or whisk until well combined.\n2. **Add the milk or cream** (if using) and season with salt and pepper.\n3. **Heat a non-stick skillet or omelette pan** over medium heat and add the butter or oil.\n4. **Pour the egg mixture** into the pan and let it cook for 1\u20132 minutes, until the edges start to set.\n5. **Use a spatula to gently lift the edges**, allowing uncooked egg to flow underneath.\n6. **Once the egg is just set but still slightly runny in the center**, add your chosen fillings (e.g., cheese, ham, spinach).\n7. **Fold the omelette in half** using the spatula and let it cook for another 1\u20132 minutes.\n8. **Slide the omelette onto a plate** and serve warm.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udca1 Tips:\n- For extra fluffiness, beat the eggs a little longer or use a whisk.\n- If your mom likes cheese, add a dollop of cream cheese or shredded cheddar.\n- For a richer flavor, use heavy cream instead of milk.\n- Pair with toast, fresh fruit, or a side of fruit salad for a complete breakfast.\n\n---\n\nAnd here's a **little secret**: If you want your omelette to look extra impressive, you can **fry the egg mixture in a small pan**, then pour it into a preheated omelette pan and cook it gently. This method gives you a fluffier texture.\n\nLet me know if you\u2019d like a **vegetarian version**, **cheese and bacon**, or even a **Spanish-style omelette** \u2014 I can tailor it to your mom\u2019s taste! \ud83e\udd50\u2764\ufe0f",
